#%PAM-1.0
# The lock screen of SherlockOS (sherlockos-lock): the password of the session's user, and
# nothing else (lot D-25l). Not `login`'s stack: its pam_nologin refuses every password once
# /run/nologin exists (five minutes before a `shutdown +N`), and its account checks have nothing
# to say to a user already logged in. The program only calls pam_authenticate, as swaylock does.
# pam_faildelay waits 3 s after a wrong password: failures are not counted, since the lock
# screen runs as the user and cannot write the counters of pam_faillock. Installed in
# /etc/pam.d/ by the author: `just install-session` prints the command.
auth     optional  pam_faildelay.so delay=3000000
auth     include   common-auth
